                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Surprisingly good game. expected nothing but got a nice brain teaser game.\n\nIdea is to get the ludoku ball moved from start to finish in a very small grid with as few moves as possible. first two episodes are for learning ánd casual play but then slowly things get tricky. play areas are small but the amount of moves required to finish is now almost constantly over 20 as you pass ep. 3 and 4.\n\n8.5/10\n\nGood game all round but some cons exist:\n\n- Lack of achievements which is quite big con as perfect solutions sometimes elude you even if you think you got the best solution. i see here great potential for some very interesting achievement hunting. No youtube videos exist so i am genuinely curious on how to perfect certain levels.\n\n- Vertical pull buttons shallow bright blue color should be better highlighted. I play on living room tv and i dont always notice when a vertical button is lit. \n\n- Gameplay is grid based so its strange that there is no gamepad support. small detail though. works fine as it is too.",
